# Release notes for v0.225.43

File: openOODA/audit/release_notes/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.43.oot

Logline: In-process Tier 1 wiring. oodac/oodac.aarch64 is a single 1.3 MB binary that handles both the text path (aarch64_emit_stream) and the AST path (aarch64_emit_direct_elf_binary) without shelling out.

Setup: ooda.pkg version=0.225.43. Tag v0.225.43.

Beats:
  1. oodac/aarch64_main.oo now imports aarch64_emit_elf.oo in addition to aarch64_emit.oo. The AST path's aarch64_emit_direct_elf_binary function is reachable from the same translation unit.
  2. The std/hw/arch_aarch64/ a64_lookup function (in aarch64_parse.oo and friends) was renamed to a64_lookup_parse to avoid a C-emit type collision with the std's other a64_lookup usages. After the rename, the in-process build succeeds with 727 unique_fns and 112 from-modules (was 251/48 with the process-spawn form).
  3. oodac/oodac.aarch64 (1,322,000 bytes, up from 635,808 with the process-spawn form) is built in one go. All four CLI forms work:
       - emit-aarch64 <file>
       - --backend aarch64 emit-aarch64 <file>
       - --ast-emit-aarch64 <file> <out.bin>
       - --backend aarch64 --ast <file> <out.bin>

What this proves:
  * The in-process Tier 1 wiring (Phase 9) is fully achieved. The process-spawn form (v0.225.39) is no longer needed; the in-process form is the canonical form.
  * The single oodac.aarch64 binary exposes the entire AArch64 surface: 25-arm dispatch ladder (text path) + AST path (aarch64_codegen.oo + aarch64_linker.oo + aarch64_emit_elf.oo).

Out of scope: oodac.aarch64.ast is now redundant (the in-process form is canonical), but is kept for backward compatibility.
